      "id": 12965,
      "name": "silopolis",
      "username": "silopolis",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silopolis/{size}/2166_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-05-04T14:30:13.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm wondering if I'm the only one, here.</p><p>I'm playing on Kindle Fire. The other day I was waiting for an appointment, and I thought, \"I'll just play some Sentinels! Knocking out Plague Rat is a great way to while away the time!\" So I loaded it up and went to start a game, and I realized that Plague Rat wasn't there! All I had was the core-game villains, heroes, and environments. Even Unity/Ambuscade/Silver Gulch were gone. I did have the Rook City variants (Old Legs, anyway), but nothing else was there.</p><p>This wasn't the first time it's happened. I know I have to redownload the expansions, and it's not that big a deal. But it's definitely a bigger deal than not having to redownload the expansions every once in a while... especially when I'm playing in waiting rooms or on a plane, when I might not have access to Wifi and am thus stuck unable to use content I paid good money for.</p><p>Is this a common problem? Is there anything I can do about this? If this is a real bug, does Handelabra know about it, and is there a fix incoming?</p><p>It's more annoying than dealbreaking, but it did turn me off of playing the app at all this weekend, since I didn't feel like sparking up my Kindle just to wait for a download to go through.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:38.884Z",
