      "raw": "<p>I&#39;m wondering if I&#39;m the only one, here.</p><p>I&#39;m playing on Kindle Fire. The other day I was waiting for an appointment, and I thought, &quot;I&#39;ll just play some Sentinels! Knocking out Plague Rat is a great way to while away the time!&quot; So I loaded it up and went to start a game, and I realized that Plague Rat wasn&#39;t there! All I had was the core-game villains, heroes, and environments. Even Unity/Ambuscade/Silver Gulch were gone. I did have the Rook City variants (Old Legs, anyway), but nothing else was there.</p><p>This wasn&#39;t the first time it&#39;s happened. I know I have to redownload the expansions, and it&#39;s not that big a deal. But it&#39;s definitely a bigger deal than not having to redownload the expansions every once in a while... especially when I&#39;m playing in waiting rooms or on a plane, when I might not have access to Wifi and am thus stuck unable to use content I paid good money for.</p><p>Is this a common problem? Is there anything I can do about this? If this is a real bug, does Handelabra know about it, and is there a fix incoming?</p><p>It&#39;s more annoying than dealbreaking, but it did turn me off of playing the app at all this weekend, since I didn&#39;t feel like sparking up my Kindle just to wait for a download to go through.</p>",
